## 2026-11-19 -- US-001: Parse role strings

Created `src/config.ts` with:
- `ROLE_OPTIONS` -- shared option definitions for -m/--model,
  --effort, --max-turns, --prefer-subagent, used by both the
  role-string parser and the yargs run command in index.ts
- `parseRoleString(input)` -- parses a role string like
  "claude -m opus --effort high --max-turns 40 --prefer-subagent"
  into a ParsedRole object using yargs in non-CLI mode with
  strict validation

Refactored `src/index.ts` to import ROLE_OPTIONS from config.ts
instead of defining the four shared options inline. This satisfies
the "shared, not copied" requirement.

Added `src/config.ts` to the second esbuild call in build-esm.
Added `test/config.test.ts` with 11 pure tests to TESTS in
scripts/test.sh. Updated AGENTS.md project structure and module
boundaries to include config.

Gotchas:
- yargs strict mode rejects bare positionals; the parser uses a
  `$0 <provider>` command pattern so the provider is consumed as
  a named positional
- `--prefer-subagent` with no value gives `""` from yargs (type
  string); the parser coerces it to `"true"` to match the AC
- tapzero `t.throws` regex matches `caught.message`, not the
  full string; yargs error messages say "Unknown argument: X"
  without the `--` prefix

## 2026-11-19 -- US-002: Load and validate .redeye.json

Added `loadConfig(root)` to `src/config.ts`:
- Reads `.redeye.json` from the given directory
- Returns `null` (loop off) when the file is missing or has
  no `adversarial` key
- When `adversarial` is present, requires `implement` and
  `review` as role strings parsed with `parseRoleString`
- Defaults `maxRounds` to 3 and `minRounds` to 1; validates
  both are positive integers and minRounds <= maxRounds
- Throws on invalid JSON, missing role, invalid role string,
  or invalid round values

Integrated into `runExecute` in `src/index.ts`:
- `loadConfig(process.cwd())` is called after ticket loading
  but before `resolveExecutable` and before any git/worktree
  work
- Errors thrown by `loadConfig` are caught by the yargs
  `.fail()` handler and routed through `formatErrorMessage`
  (exit 2, no stack trace)

Added 12 pure tests to `test/config.test.ts` covering all
validation paths. Added 3 CLI tests to
`test/integration.test.ts`:
- Invalid JSON exits 2 with no integration branch
- Role string with unsupported flag exits 2 with no branch
- `pi --max-turns 40` in a role string passes `--dry-run`

Added a `.redeye.json` section to README describing the file
shape and role-string syntax.

Gotchas:
- The loaded config is currently unused (`_adversarial`);
  later stories (US-004+) will wire it into the run
- `loadConfig` throws, not returns an error, so the yargs
  async handler's rejection routes it to `.fail(null, err)`
  which does `formatErrorMessage` + exit 2

## 2026-11-19 -- US-003: Show the config in --dry-run

Added adversarial config display to the --dry-run output in
`src/index.ts`. When `.redeye.json` has an `adversarial` key,
--dry-run prints the implement role string, review role string,
maxRounds and minRounds, each on its own labeled line, right
after the Provider line and before the wave/branch output.

Added `implementStr` and `reviewStr` fields to
`AdversarialConfig` in `src/config.ts` to preserve the
original role strings from the config file.

Added two CLI tests in `test/integration.test.ts`:
- With adversarial configured, the four values appear in stdout
- Without adversarial, no Implement or maxRounds lines appear

Gotchas:
- The dry-run adversarial block prints before both the
  isolated and non-isolated branches, so it appears in both
  paths

## 2026-11-19 -- US-004: A bare redeye uses the implement role

Made the run command's provider positional optional (`$0 [provider]
[turns]`). When `.redeye.json` sets an adversarial implement role
and no CLI provider is given, the implement role's provider and
model are used. A CLI provider overrides implement and logs a
one-liner; `--dry-run` repeats the override. Without config and
without a provider, the usage error is unchanged (exit 1 with help
text).

Changes in `src/index.ts`:
- `.check()` validates no-config + no-provider, throws a clear
  Error that yargs routes to .fail() as a usage error (exit 1,
  help text shown)
- `runExecute` resolves `provider` and `model` from the implement
  role when no CLI provider is given
- `cliOverride` flag logs the override before provider lookup
- dry-run block prints the override line
- The resolved adversarial review role is threaded through to
  `runWavesIsolated` as an `adversarial` option, but no reviewer
  is started yet

Changes in `src/orchestrator.ts`:
- `runWavesIsolated` gains an optional `adversarial` parameter
  carrying the parsed review role, maxRounds and minRounds, for
  later stories to consume

Added three CLI tests in `test/integration.test.ts`:
- Bare redeye with adversarial config uses implement provider in
  --dry-run
- CLI provider overrides implement in --dry-run
- No config and no provider exits 1 with help text

README already documents the optional provider in the flags table
and in the .redeye.json section from US-002/US-003.

Gotchas:
- yargs `.check()` throws an Error whose message arrives as
  fail(msg, err, yargs), so both msg and err are truthy -- the
  fail handler's `if (err && !msg)` branch is NOT taken, help
  text IS shown, and exit code is 1. This matches the AC

## 2026-11-19 -- US-005: Merge role-string flags with run-wide CLI flags

Added `mergeRoleWithCli(role, cli)` to `src/config.ts`:
- Pure function that merges a ParsedRole with CLI options
- Role-string flags win over CLI flags for the same field
- CLI flags fill in whatever the role string leaves out
- Applies independently per role (implement and review)

Also exported the `CliOptions` interface for the CLI-side fields
(model, effort, maxTurns, preferSubagent).

Added 5 pure tests to `test/config.test.ts`:
- Role flag wins over CLI flag
- CLI fills in missing fields
- Role with all fields ignores CLI entirely
- Empty CLI leaves role unchanged
- Applies separately to implement and review roles
